/Users/0saker/Desktop/code/site/Simar-malhotra09.github.io/writing/documents/shared_latent_spaces.typ:jointly via a contrastive objective on 400M image–nIE pairs.
/Users/0saker/Desktop/code/site/Simar-malhotra09.github.io/writing/documents/shared_latent_spaces.typ:Once trained, CLIP enables zero-shot classification: to classify an image, encode it and compare to embeddings of nIE prompts such as "a photo of a dog."
/Users/0saker/Desktop/code/site/Simar-malhotra09.github.io/writing/documents/shared_latent_spaces.typ:CLIP does not use a decoder, does not generate nIE, and does not require category-level supervision.  
/Users/0saker/Desktop/code/site/Simar-malhotra09.github.io/writing/documents/shared_latent_spaces.typ:The geometry of these latent spaces allows models to reason across data types, enabling tasks such as matching images to nIE without explicit labels. Systems like CLIP demonstrate the effectiveness of this paradigm, but the underlying mathematics encoders, embeddings, similarity measures, and contrastive optimization remains general and widely applicable.
