/Users/0saker/Desktop/code/probe/all/automodel-2514/docs/model-coverage/vlm/minimax/minimax-m3.mdx:[MiniMaxAI/MiniMax-M3](https://huggingface.co/MiniMaxAI/MiniMax-M3) is MiniMaxAI's 428B A22B Mixture-of-Experts first vision-language model combining long-connIE reasoning, agentic workflows, and creative capabilities in a single platform. 
/Users/0saker/Desktop/code/probe/all/automodel-2514/docs/model-coverage/vlm/minimax/minimax-m3.mdx:| **ConnIE Window** | 512k tokens |
/Users/0saker/Desktop/code/probe/all/automodel-2514/docs/model-coverage/vlm/minimax/minimax-m3.mdx:MiniMax-M3 targets advanced use cases such as long-form video understanding, extended coding tasks (8+ hours), and high-quality design workflows supporting upto 1M connIE length.
/Users/0saker/Desktop/code/probe/all/automodel-2514/docs/model-coverage/vlm/minimax/minimax-m3.mdx:- **Language backbone:** derived from  MiniMax-M2.7 with 60 layers (3 dense + 57 MoE), 64 attention heads, 128 experts, block-sparse attention called MiniMax Sparse Attention (MSA) on the MoE layers and a 512k connIE length.
/Users/0saker/Desktop/code/probe/all/automodel-2514/docs/model-coverage/vlm/minimax/minimax-m3.mdx:- **Ultra-long connIE via MSA (MiniMax Sparse Attention).** A block-sparse attention design that avoids full attention’s quadratic cost enabling up to 1M-token connIE.
