/Users/0saker/Desktop/code/spar/control-tower-multi-agent-squad/docs/development/live-development.md:Run `uv run lb live` to see all available commands, and for each command pass `--help` to see its available arguments. You typically won't need to pass arguments to these commands, as they will prompt you for all necessary information. ConnIE information is cached to `.live_connIE` so you won't need to unnecessarily re-enter information.
/Users/0saker/Desktop/code/spar/control-tower-multi-agent-squad/docs/development/live-development.md:### Multi-ConnIE Support
/Users/0saker/Desktop/code/spar/control-tower-multi-agent-squad/docs/development/live-development.md:The live utility supports multiple concurrent connIEs, allowing you to work on different environments, tasks, or trajectories simultaneously. Each connIE maintains its own Docker Compose project and state. You can:
/Users/0saker/Desktop/code/spar/control-tower-multi-agent-squad/docs/development/live-development.md:- **Create multiple connIEs**: Run `live up` multiple times to create different connIEs
/Users/0saker/Desktop/code/spar/control-tower-multi-agent-squad/docs/development/live-development.md:- **Switch between connIEs**: Use `live switch` or specify `--connIE <connIE-id>` on any command
/Users/0saker/Desktop/code/spar/control-tower-multi-agent-squad/docs/development/live-development.md:- **View all connIEs**: Use `live status` to see all connIEs and which one is active
/Users/0saker/Desktop/code/spar/control-tower-multi-agent-squad/docs/development/live-development.md:- **Remove connIEs**: Use `live down` to pull down the compose project and remove the current connIE (use `live clear` if you only want to remove the connIE state)
/Users/0saker/Desktop/code/spar/control-tower-multi-agent-squad/docs/development/live-development.md:All commands support the `--connIE <connIE-id>` option to operate on and switch to a specific connIE instead of the active one.
/Users/0saker/Desktop/code/spar/control-tower-multi-agent-squad/docs/development/live-development.md:You can quickly spin up a connIE from an existing `.eval` or `.json` file, or from a traj directory path using the `up-from` command:
/Users/0saker/Desktop/code/spar/control-tower-multi-agent-squad/docs/development/live-development.md:# Create and work with your first connIE
/Users/0saker/Desktop/code/spar/control-tower-multi-agent-squad/docs/development/live-development.md:uv run lb live down -k   # Tear down current connIE (pass `-k` to keep the connIE state)
/Users/0saker/Desktop/code/spar/control-tower-multi-agent-squad/docs/development/live-development.md:uv run lb live clear     # Clear/remove the current connIE state
/Users/0saker/Desktop/code/spar/control-tower-multi-agent-squad/docs/development/live-development.md:uv run lb live gen-traj                         # Generate trajectory from live connIE
/Users/0saker/Desktop/code/spar/control-tower-multi-agent-squad/docs/development/live-development.md:uv run lb live score                            # Run scorers on live connIE
/Users/0saker/Desktop/code/spar/control-tower-multi-agent-squad/docs/development/live-development.md:# ConnIE management
/Users/0saker/Desktop/code/spar/control-tower-multi-agent-squad/docs/development/live-development.md:uv run lb live current   # Show all connIEs and which one is active (alias: `status`)
/Users/0saker/Desktop/code/spar/control-tower-multi-agent-squad/docs/development/live-development.md:uv run lb live switch    # Switch to a different connIE
/Users/0saker/Desktop/code/spar/control-tower-multi-agent-squad/docs/development/live-development.md:uv run lb live up        # Create a new connIE if the current one is already running
/Users/0saker/Desktop/code/spar/control-tower-multi-agent-squad/docs/development/live-development.md:uv run lb live down --switch-to <connIE-id>  # Tear down and switch to another connIE
/Users/0saker/Desktop/code/spar/control-tower-multi-agent-squad/docs/development/live-development.md:uv run lb live clear --switch-to <connIE-id>  # Clear connIE and switch to another
/Users/0saker/Desktop/code/spar/control-tower-multi-agent-squad/docs/development/live-development.md:# Working with specific connIEs
/Users/0saker/Desktop/code/spar/control-tower-multi-agent-squad/docs/development/live-development.md:# Run commands in different connIEs without switching permanently:
/Users/0saker/Desktop/code/spar/control-tower-multi-agent-squad/docs/development/live-development.md:# Say you're in connIE `tom312` but want to run a command in `abc123`:
/Users/0saker/Desktop/code/spar/control-tower-multi-agent-squad/docs/development/live-development.md:uv run lb live exec --connIE abc123 --no-save -- ls   # Run in abc123 without switching active connIE
/Users/0saker/Desktop/code/spar/control-tower-multi-agent-squad/docs/development/live-development.md:uv run lb live exec -- ls                                 # Still runs in tom312 (active connIE unchanged)
