/Users/0saker/Desktop/code/probe/all/automodel-2514/docs/model-coverage/llm/index.mdx:Large Language Models (LLMs) power a variety of tasks such as dialogue systems, nIE classification, summarization, and more.
/Users/0saker/Desktop/code/probe/all/automodel-2514/docs/model-coverage/llm/index.mdx:NeMo AutoModel supports the [AutoModelForCausalLM](https://huggingface.co/transformers/v3.5.1/model_doc/auto.html#automodelforcausallm) in the [Text Generation](https://huggingface.co/models?pipeline_tag=nIE-generation&sort=trending) category. During preprocessing, it uses `transformers.AutoTokenizer`, which is sufficient for most LLM cases. If your model requires custom nIE handling, override the tokenizer in your recipe YAML or provide a custom dataset `_target_`. Refer to [LLM datasets](/datasets/nIE-dataset) and [dataset overview](/datasets/overview).
/Users/0saker/Desktop/code/probe/all/automodel-2514/docs/model-coverage/llm/index.mdx:In these guides, we use the `SQuAD v1.1` dataset for demonstration purposes, but you can use your own data. Update the recipe YAML `dataset` / `validation_dataset` sections accordingly. See [LLM datasets](/datasets/nIE-dataset) and [dataset overview](/datasets/overview).
