/Users/0saker/Desktop/code/spar/control-tower-multi-agent-squad/docs/development/strajs/workflow.md:You should start by spinning up a live connIE with the relevant parameters. A traj directory with a template and description file will be created automatically:
/Users/0saker/Desktop/code/spar/control-tower-multi-agent-squad/docs/development/strajs/workflow.md:Then get to work on developing a straj. If your idea involves file edits (which it likely does), you can make your changes in the fresh mounted directory at `container_mounts/{connIE_id}/app`. `connIE_id` refers to the active live connIE id, accessible via `live status`.
/Users/0saker/Desktop/code/spar/control-tower-multi-agent-squad/docs/development/strajs/workflow.md:Then you can reflect on what commands you ran (if any) to assist in your solution, and copy them to your `template.jsonl` as bash commands in the correct order. Note that by default, bash commands will be placed after the nIE_editor file edit commands when you generate the solution trajectory. If you need more control over command ordering, you can optionally use placeholders in the template trajectory to specify exactly where file edit tool calls should appear. Make sure the file paths are correct if you do this and use absolute paths.
/Users/0saker/Desktop/code/spar/control-tower-multi-agent-squad/docs/development/strajs/workflow.md:Whenever you want to tear down and re-up the container/connIE state, here is the process you should follow:
/Users/0saker/Desktop/code/spar/control-tower-multi-agent-squad/docs/development/strajs/workflow.md:4. Then you can run `uv run lb live traj` to run each tool call in your solution trajectory, bringing the container state to where it should be after each tool call in the solution traj has been run. If you just want to update the files and not run any bash tool calls, you can pass `--include-tool nIE_editor` to `uv run lb live traj`.
/Users/0saker/Desktop/code/spar/control-tower-multi-agent-squad/docs/development/strajs/workflow.md:One approach you might think of is to run `uv run lb live down` with `--keep-fresh-mount-dir`, and pass in the kept directory to `--mount-dir` on `uv run lb live up`. The problem with this is that on setup, the system will initialize git at this already changed codebase state. Thus, when you run `gen-traj`, the git diff used to generate the nIE_editor tool calls will not register the previous changes you were hoping to preserve.
/Users/0saker/Desktop/code/spar/control-tower-multi-agent-squad/docs/development/strajs/workflow.md:You shouldn't need to manually update the files again in the mounted directory. This wastes your connIE. Instead, make sure you follow this approach of running `uv run lb live traj --include-tool nIE_editor` to get back to the previous file state.
