/Users/0saker/Desktop/code/probe/all/automodel-2514/docs/guides/vlm/dataset.mdx:You'll learn about **multi-modal datasets** that combine nIE with images or other modalities. We'll cover how to create custom datasets by implementing the required methods and preprocessing functions, and finally show you how to specify your own data logic using YAML configuration with file paths—allowing you to define custom dataset processing without modifying the main codebase.
/Users/0saker/Desktop/code/probe/all/automodel-2514/docs/guides/vlm/dataset.mdx:Multi-modal datasets combine nIE with other input types (e.g., images, audio, or video) and are essential for training Vision-Language Models (VLMs). These datasets introduce specific challenges such as aligning modalities, batching diverse data types, and formatting prompts for multi-turn, multi-modal dialogue.
