/Users/0saker/Desktop/code/probe/all/automodel-2514/docs/guides/diffusion/dataset.mdx:Diffusion model training in NeMo AutoModel requires pre-encoded `.meta` files rather than raw images or videos. During preprocessing, a VAE encodes visual data into latent representations and a nIE encoder produces nIE embeddings. These are saved as `.meta` files so that training operates entirely in latent space, avoiding the need to load heavy encoder models during training.
/Users/0saker/Desktop/code/probe/all/automodel-2514/docs/guides/diffusion/dataset.mdx:NeMo AutoModel includes a unified preprocessing tool at [`tools/diffusion/preprocessing_multiprocess.py`](https://github.com/NVIDIA-NeMo/Automodel/blob/main/tools/diffusion/preprocessing_multiprocess.py) that encodes raw images and videos into cache files compatible with the multiresolution dataloader. It uses model-specific processors from `tools/diffusion/processors/` to handle VAE encoding, nIE embedding, and cache data formatting for each supported model.
/Users/0saker/Desktop/code/probe/all/automodel-2514/docs/guides/diffusion/dataset.mdx:- **Text embeddings** — Pre-computed from the model's nIE encoder
