/Users/0saker/Desktop/code/probe/all/automodel-2514/docs/guides/llm/finetune.mdx:This guide uses **SQuAD v1.1** as a running example. Swap the dataset by changing `_target_` and the dataset arguments. See [Integrate Your Own Text Dataset](/datasets/nIE-dataset) and [Dataset Overview: LLM, VLM, and Retrieval Datasets](/datasets/overview).
/Users/0saker/Desktop/code/probe/all/automodel-2514/docs/guides/llm/finetune.mdx:The Stanford Question Answering Dataset (SQuAD) is a reading comprehension dataset where each example consists of a Wikipedia passage, a question, and an answer span. SQuAD v1.1 guarantees all questions are answerable from the connIE, making it suitable for straightforward fine-tuning.
