/Users/0saker/Desktop/code/probe/all/automodel-2514/examples/speculative/dspark/gemma4_12b_dspark.yaml:# Gemma4 target's nIE sub-config. Feature layers and mask token id follow the
/Users/0saker/Desktop/code/probe/all/automodel-2514/docs/guides/llm/hy3.mdx:[tencent/Hy3-preview](https://huggingface.co/tencent/Hy3-preview) is a 295B Mixture-of-Experts language model from Tencent. It features 80 transformer layers (layer 0 dense, layers 1–79 MoE), 192 routed experts plus one shared expert per MoE block with top-8 sigmoid routing, Grouped Query Attention (64 Q / 8 KV heads, `head_dim=128`), per-head QK RMSNorm applied before RoPE, and an `expert_bias` buffer (surfaced as `e_score_correction_bias` in the Automodel gate) for expert-load correction during inference. The model supports a 256K connIE window via long-connIE RoPE (`rope_theta=11158840`).
/Users/0saker/Desktop/code/probe/all/automodel-2514/docs/guides/llm/hy3.mdx:We use [HellaSwag](https://huggingface.co/datasets/Rowan/hellaswag), a commonsense natural-language-inference dataset consisting of connIE + four candidate continuations. The version used here is the standard `rowan/hellaswag` HuggingFace split, formatted for next-token-prediction fine-tuning.
/Users/0saker/Desktop/code/probe/all/automodel-2514/docs/guides/llm/hy3.mdx:- **Long-connIE RoPE**: `rope_theta=11158840` with dynamic NTK-aware scaling (`beta_slow` / `beta_fast`) extending the connIE to 256K tokens.
