/Users/0saker/Desktop/code/probe/all/automodel-2514/docs/guides/llm/dataset.mdx:**Instruction datasets** are question-answer pairs where the model learns to respond to specific instructions or questions. These datasets are structured as connIE-question pairs with corresponding answers, making them ideal for teaching models to follow instructions and provide accurate responses.
/Users/0saker/Desktop/code/probe/all/automodel-2514/docs/guides/llm/dataset.mdx:- **ConnIE**: A paragraph of nIE from Wikipedia
/Users/0saker/Desktop/code/probe/all/automodel-2514/docs/guides/llm/dataset.mdx:- **Question**: A question about the connIE
/Users/0saker/Desktop/code/probe/all/automodel-2514/docs/guides/llm/dataset.mdx:- **Answers**: The correct answer with its position in the connIE
/Users/0saker/Desktop/code/probe/all/automodel-2514/docs/guides/llm/dataset.mdx:The [`squad.py`](https://github.com/NVIDIA-NeMo/Automodel/blob/main/nemo_automodel/components/datasets/llm/squad.py) file contains the implementation for processing the SQuAD dataset into a format suitable for instruction tuning. It defines a dataset class and preprocessing functions that extract the connIE, question, and answer fields, concatenate them into a prompt-completion format, and apply tokenization, padding, and loss masking. This serves as a template for building custom instruction datasets by following a similar structure and adapting the extraction logic to your dataset's schema.
/Users/0saker/Desktop/code/probe/all/automodel-2514/docs/guides/llm/dataset.mdx:NeMo AutoModel supports **packed sequences**, which is a technique to optimize training with variable-length sequences (such as nIE) by minimizing padding.
/Users/0saker/Desktop/code/probe/all/automodel-2514/docs/guides/llm/dataset.mdx:- They are especially useful for language modeling and nIE datasets.
