/Users/0saker/Desktop/code/probe/all/automodel-2514/docs/guides/llm/nemotron-3-ultra.md:[nvidia/NVIDIA-Nemotron-3-Ultra-550B-A55B-BF16](https://huggingface.co/nvidia/NVIDIA-Nemotron-3-Ultra-550B-A55B-BF16) is a frontier-scale large language model (LLM) trained by NVIDIA, designed to deliver strong agentic, reasoning, and conversational capabilities. It is optimized for the most demanding workloads, including complex multi-step agents, long-connIE analysis, and high-accuracy reasoning over code, math, and science. Like other models in the family, it responds to user queries and tasks by first generating a reasoning trace and then concluding with a final response. The model's reasoning capabilities can be configured through a flag in the chat template.
/Users/0saker/Desktop/code/probe/all/automodel-2514/docs/guides/llm/nemotron-3-ultra.md:The model employs a hybrid Latent Mixture-of-Experts (LatentMoE) architecture, utilizing interleaved Mamba-2 and MoE layers, along with select Attention layers. Like the Super model, the Ultra model incorporates Multi-Token Prediction (MTP) layers for faster nIE generation and improved quality, and it is trained using an NVFP4 pre-training recipe to maximize compute efficiency. The model has 55B active parameters and 550B parameters in total.
/Users/0saker/Desktop/code/probe/all/automodel-2514/docs/guides/llm/nemotron-3-ultra.md:We use [HellaSwag](https://huggingface.co/datasets/Rowan/hellaswag), a commonsense natural-language-inference dataset consisting of connIE + four candidate continuations. The version used here is the standard `rowan/hellaswag` HuggingFace split, formatted for next-token-prediction fine-tuning.
